Notes on things from the spec I did not implement (or implemented approximately):

- **Entry-path shapes and dive/escort curves** are hand-tuned Bézier approximations rather than the exact arcade path tables; escort dives work but escorts follow the boss rigidly rather than peeling off on their own curves.
- **Challenge-stage looping patterns** are five generic loop paths (not the exact five arcade wave patterns); wave bonuses are folded into the final "NUMBER OF HITS" tally line rather than announced per wave (the 1,000-per-wave and 10,000 PERFECT bonuses are scored, but only the perfect bonus is shown in the text).
- The **captured fighter turning "hostile"** when its formation boss is shot is represented by it being destroyed with an explosion (it never returns), rather than flying off as an active shooter.
- **Sound effects are synthesized approximations** of the arcade originals (waveform envelopes, not exact samples), and the stage-start jingle is a short original fanfare.
- The captured fighter fires only while its boss is in the tractor-beam dive (spec's "when its Boss dives" read as the beam dive); a captive does not fire during plain boss dives.
